<html><head><title>Are you stuck?</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px"><p style="color: windowtext"><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">Every transdisciplinary project reaches a moment when doubt sets in, frustration rises, and the guiding vision seems lost. This is sometimes referred to as </span><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold">“Blue Monday.”</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px"><p style="color: windowtext"><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">&nbsp;If you’ve reached that point, you can use the following questions and exercises to regain perspective.*</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px"><p style="color: windowtext"><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">Under the </span><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold">practice tab</span><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">, you’ll find a series of questions and assignments designed to help you get back on track, based on a card game by Ankie Schoemakers, adapted by Meike Koop (from the </span><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; font-style: italic; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">Mind the Gap</span><span lang="NL-NL" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif"> research group at Avans University of Applied Sciences, led by Henk Spies).</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 25.575px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p></div></body></html>